      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a laissez-faire approach maximizes efficiency in some sectors, history shows that unchecked markets can lead to monopolies and public safety failures that only regulation can prevent. Most experts suggest a hybrid model where core safety standards are enforced to protect consumers, while bureaucratic red tape is significantly reduced to foster competition. Relying solely on the market to judge safety may result in short-term gains for corporations but long-term risks to society.",
      "source": "target",
